abstract: >-
  An interactive 3D web-based astronomical simulator that reconstructs and
  compares the mathematical planetary models of the 14th-century Damascus
  astronomer Ala al-Din Ali ibn al-Shatir (d. 1375 CE / 777 AH) with those
  of Ptolemy, Copernicus, and Kepler. Features include a full Three.js
  celestial dome, Islamic prayer time calculations using the historical
  Sine Quadrant (Rub' al-Mujayyab) method, seasonal declination arcs,
  twilight depression circles, and a database of 465+ world cities.
  The simulator demonstrates Ibn al-Shatir's revolutionary elimination
  of the Ptolemaic equant and eccentric, achieving uniform circular motion
  through his double-epicycle mechanism — the same geometric construction
  later adopted by Copernicus.
